    ["这双靴子走过太多地方了，多到它能和自己的所有者和平共处。\n有人穿着它在婚礼的酒渍中起舞，有人带着它在庆典的花瓣中大笑，有人喜欢在潮声里踏入碎银般的海浪，有人怕它磨损，就装入玻璃做的展示盒。\n和女孩一起埋在废墟下时，它表面的符文还和刚附着时一样精美。\n“如果谁能记得我就好了。”\n它总觉得，很久以前也有人这么说过。"] = "These boots have walked through too many places, so many that they could coexist peacefully with their owners. \n Some wore them to dance amidst the wine stains of a wedding, some carried them to laugh among the petals of a celebration, some liked to step into the silver-like sea waves amidst the sound of the tide, and some were afraid of wearing them out, so they placed them in a glass display case. \n When buried under the ruins with the girl, the runes on their surface were as exquisite as when they were first attached. \n \"If only someone could remember me.\" \n It always felt that someone had said this a long time ago.",
